      "side": 1,
      "message": "The scope of fsal_fd_total_counter is not just for reporting. The current LRU logic uses fsal_fd_global_counter for FD pressure detection, which does not account for STATE and TEMP FDs.\n\nPlease refer to the following patch for the LRU issue and rationale:\n\nhttps://review.gerrithub.io/c/ffilz/nfs-ganesha/+/1247084\n\nAlso, the additional atomic increment/decrement is only performed during FD lifecycle operations such as insert_fd_lru() / remove_fd_lru(). It is not added to the normal NFS operation paths such as read, write, lookup, getattr, setattr, or lock. Therefore, this is not really a hot path.",
